# proc-memstat review round 1, P4-2 — three-scan vs one-scan /proc/self/status
# reader cost, and the saving expressed over one whole snapshot() call.
#
# Measured on GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest (the `measure — three-scan vs
# one-scan /proc/self/status cost (P4-2)` step of the `proc-memstat gates
# (ubuntu-latest)` job). This box is Windows and has no /proc at all, and it
# runs agents under a 5% CPU cap, so a local run measures scheduling, not the
# reader.
#
# Reproduce:
#   cargo run --release -p proc-memstat --example status_scan_cost
#
# TRUNCATED — the surrounding job log (checkout, toolchain, fmt, clippy, test,
# rustdoc, link-smoke, package steps) is omitted; only the measurement step's
# own stdout is kept. Full job logs are reproducible from the run IDs cited
# below until GitHub expires them (90 days), and from the command above
# indefinitely.

